          "section": "CI37262802366 sentence ('Linux218 pass/29 typed-refusal fail/16 ignored')",
          "causal_reproduction": "The CI evidence JSON records a single test_results line: '218 passed; 29 failed; 16 ignored'. This is the first (lib) test binary. Because `cargo test --locked --workspace` aborts after the first failing binary, the adapter/context/grok/integration/doctest binaries never ran on Linux. Locally those binaries contributed 19+14+9 failures. A reader can take 'Linux218 pass/29 fail' as a complete Linux workspace result and infer that the 133 non-policy local failures are absent on Linux, which is unproven.",
          "source_basis": "issue-9-formal-refusal-source1-ci.json test_results has exactly one line. Compare issue-9-formal-refusal-source1.json, where the full local run lists separate lib/adapter/context/grok binaries. The Ubuntu step 6 fails, and steps 7 and 8 are skipped.",
          "minimal_fix": "Wording only: say 'Linux lib binary 218 pass/29 typed-refusal fail/16 ignored; remaining workspace binaries did not execute after that failure'. Make no attribution or nonregression claim for the unexecuted binaries. No source or test change."
        }
